comments.body:
Independent confirmation on `main` @ `7daa3ab` (Windows 11, Python 3.12.14, `InMemorySaver` — no external services needed).

The MRE reproduces exactly as reported: the first invoke returns a tuple, `get_state()` already shows the list, the second invoke raises `TypeError: can only concatenate list (not "tuple") to list`, and every subsequent call on the thread fails the same way.

I also verified the scoped fix proposed in this issue, applied to `BinaryOperatorAggregate.from_checkpoint` via the existing `_strip_extras` helper:

- `get_state()` returns the declared `tuple` again, and the second invoke succeeds;
- the `set` path from #8388 still reproduces untouched — the wire format is unchanged, so #8388 remains with its reporter;
- `tests/test_channels.py`, `tests/test_state.py` and `tests/test_delta_channel_migration.py` all pass with the change (68 passed).

@Hotragn has the complete fix and said they'll open the PR once assigned — I'm not opening a competing PR; supporting their assignment. (Edit: corrected the handle — I had pinged @To3akaRin, the reporter of #9087, by mistake.)
